# Isolated RSM bridge preparation

Actual author `/root/formal_oracle`. This is a prospective integration proposal,
with handwritten test inputs only. It does not install code, generate a cohort,
read a producer reference, validate production data, or approve a release.

The operative task has exactly nine fields: `kind,version,initial_state,options,
entry,mode,history,checkpoint,event_budget`. All control metadata stays outside
that task and the student prompt. The public batch is
`option-resumption-pilot-v1`; no exact generator-version spelling is prescribed.
The prototype treats revision strings as broad routing cues only, never as
proof of validity or a new closed acceptance grammar.

The original checker must stay at
`reviews/oracle/RSM-option-resumption-corpus-20261010T0956Z/corpus_checker_attempt04.py`
(`bdbc7287d5a9167013c21665f4793457481db55612fc9e60fef11fa7157fb9a9`).
Its `ROOT=parents[3]` and both immutable dependencies are checked before import
and again after proof calls. The proposed shared adapter will be a NEW source
version of this isolated prototype with an explicitly correct factory-root
binding. Neither this preparation file nor bdbc is blindly relocated.

Future installation, only after separate root authorization and backup proof:

1. Add a factory bridge that loads the original checker at its exact path.
   Broader routing selects by the public batch, task kind, optional RSM revision
   cue or published unique control names. Once selected, retain every supplied
   row: no filtering by current kind, version, track, claims, context or approval
   flag. The public closed216 cohort and actual original candidate membership
   are hard gates. Malformed labels, missing metadata and approval subsets fail.
   If every routing cue and external source/batch identity is simultaneously
   erased, identity cannot be inferred from arbitrary IDs; preserve the public
   batch in the release manifest/source registry rather than inventing ID syntax.
2. Route the independent target to own immutable official427 interpreter.
   Producer reference routing must use a separately authored implementation;
   none is imported or emulated as independent reference here. Legacy skills
   and other kinds continue through the existing dispatch unchanged. Typed
   agreement with that separate reference remains NOT_RUN in this preparation.
3. In `factory.pipeline.audit`, add row checks and a full raw-evidence control
   report. Record the source/byte ledger, author, actual runner, errors/counts,
   targets, control proofs and novelty diagnostics; preserve all previous audit
   bytes before replacing current machine evidence. Include the RSM control
   error count in `batch_control_failure_count` and quality status.
4. In `release`, enforce RSM full controls on the original candidate and again
   on all accepted projections after receipt filtering, before `dest.mkdir`.
   Missing even one approved row blocks the entire closed cohort. Existing
   independent expert/red/adjudication decisions remain separate requirements.
5. In `validate_release`, repeat full RSM custody/control proofs on all current
   accepted rows with the preserved exact PENDING candidate bytes. The manifest
   candidate SHA is not the accepted canonical-file SHA. Only the four existing
   review/lineage fields may change; current full hashes remain checked.
6. Guard direct `factory.exports.specialized` and `write_specialized` before
   selecting a split or opening a file. Guard direct
   `factory.export_validation.validate_specialized` with the same full cohort.
   RSM `skill_demonstrations` retains the existing input/target format. Both
   split outputs must total216 and have exact typed one-per-row coverage.
   Full SFT/structured coverage remains independently checked. A release-only
   hook is insufficient because these functions can be called directly.

The loader consumes safe ROOT-relative regular files using no-follow path
descriptors. It loads complete original PENDING216 bytes first, obtains every
manifest path from those original claims, then loads all six public sources,
every asserted additional source, exact raw manifests and the frozen target-free
legacy bytes. Missing/changed/unsafe bytes return UNKNOWN errors. It rehashes
every observed file after the proof. No ambient candidate or target fallback,
canonical manifest hash, global control-ID uniqueness, required optional member
hash or private ID grammar is introduced.

The existing `release` source globs omit reviews and curriculum files. Explicitly
append the bridge, original bdbc checker, official427, graphbb628, all six public
sources/configuration, canonical schema, target-free legacy bytes and all
runtime asserted source dependencies. Archive their exact raw bytes under
`reproducibility/source_blobs/{sha}.source` and record original relative paths.
Restoration must reconstruct those paths before import. Exact pending candidate
and raw manifest custody belong in the release's input/evidence ledger. Do not
pretend a source hash alone preserves a missing file. The isolated package
demonstrator writes only below this NEW preparation prefix.

The new gate tests use the already exposed handmade216 records and original
manifest, never producer data. Any failed source/import/test is immutable and
superseded only by a fresh version. Shared author/model and solver dependency
correlation are disclosed. Difficulty-level semantic review, whole production
novelty, separate reference agreement, full reviewer predictions, publication,
integration/full-suite execution and remote backup proof are not claimed here.
